# Verible style-lint ruleset for chi_to_cxl_bridge (passed via --rules_config).
#
# The rules below are DISABLED as documented, intentional house-style deviations
# — not defects. Every other Verible rule stays enabled, so `make verible-lint`
# is a real style gate for the rest. Rationale per rule:
#
#   line-length            Dense single-line FORMAL assertions, the packed-flit
#                          field tables in chi_to_cxl_bridge_defs.vh, and the
#                          translate_* functions are deliberately wide.
#   always-comb            The infra modules (async_fifo, reset_drain, ...) use
#                          `always @(*)` and are byte-identical to the proven
#                          cxl_lpddr5x_bridge copies — see doc/PLAN.md Notes; they
#                          must not diverge, so this is not reformatted.
#   explicit-parameter-storage-type / parameter-name-style /
#   unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
#                          Same proven-infra constraint (localparam masks/counts,
#                          `mem[0:DEPTH-1]` memories), plus the defs field-offset
#                          localparams; kept in the workspace's established style.
-line-length
-always-comb
-explicit-parameter-storage-type
-parameter-name-style
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
